{"absent":["Locking discipline for identifier tables and concurrent matching","State machines for bus enumeration, probing and driver binding","Matching algorithms using flags, masks, ranges and wildcards","Module loading and modalias string generation beyond templates","Allocation and lifetime of pointed-to data such as names and driver pointers","Endianness, packing guarantees and user ABI stability beyond shown attributes"],"dossier":"D17","findings":[{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/dfl.h::dfl_device_id"],"text":"DFL identification entry pairs two small unsigned selectors distinguishing device kind and feature number with a word sized opaque value reserved for driver use."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/dmi.h::dmi_field","include/linux/device-id/dmi.h::dmi_strmatch","include/linux/device-id/dmi.h::dmi_system_id"],"text":"DMI identification uses a slot enumeration spanning firmware, system, board and chassis attributes with a maximum sentinel and a special OEM string case, a substring matcher holding a seven bit slot selector plus an exactness flag and a fixed length text buffer, and a table entry holding a match callback, an identification label, four such matchers and an opaque driver pointer."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/dmi.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_DMI_H","include/linux/device-id/dmi.h::DMI_MATCH","include/linux/device-id/dmi.h::DMI_EXACT_MATCH","include/linux/device-id/dmi.h::dmi_device_id"],"text":"Two construction helpers build a single DMI matcher from slot and substring, one requesting substring comparison and the other requesting exact comparison; the DMI device identifier name is an alias of the system identifier structure."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/eisa.h::eisa_device_id","include/linux/device-id/fsl_mc.h::fsl_mc_device_id","include/linux/device-id/hda.h::hda_device_id"],"text":"EISA entries hold a fixed length signature plus driver context; FSL-MC entries hold a sixteen bit vendor code plus a sixteen character object type string; HDA entries hold vendor and revision codes plus an API version byte, a name pointer and driver context."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/eisa.h::EISA_SIG_LEN","include/linux/device-id/eisa.h::EISA_DEVICE_MODALIAS_FMT"],"text":"EISA signature length is eight characters; EISA modalias joins letters e i s a with colon, letter s and a string placeholder."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/hid.h::hid_device_id","include/linux/device-id/hv_vmbus.h::hv_vmbus_device_id","include/linux/device-id/i2c.h::i2c_device_id","include/linux/device-id/mcb.h::mcb_device_id","include/linux/device-id/ishtp.h::ishtp_device_id"],"text":"HID entries carry bus and group selectors plus vendor and product codes and driver context; Hyper-V VMBus and ISHTP entries pair a globally unique identifier with driver context; I2C entries pair a short fixed length name with driver context; MCB entries pair a sixteen bit device code with driver context."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/hid.h::HID_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/hid.h::HID_BUS_ANY","include/linux/device-id/hid.h::HID_GROUP_ANY","include/linux/device-id/ipack.h::IPACK_ANY_FORMAT","include/linux/device-id/ipack.h::IPACK_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/isapnp.h::ISAPNP_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/pci.h::PCI_ANY_ID"],"text":"Several buses define wildcards meaning match any: HID uses all bits set for identifier and all bits set in sixteen bits for bus with zero for group; IPACK uses 255 for format and all bits set for identifiers; ISA PnP uses all bits set in sixteen bits; PCI uses all bits set in thirty-two bits."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/i3c.h::i3c_device_id","include/linux/device-id/ieee1394.h::ieee1394_device_id","include/linux/device-id/ieee1394.h::ieee1394_device_id.anon_1","include/linux/device-id/ipack.h::ipack_device_id","include/linux/device-id/isapnp.h::isapnp_device_id"],"text":"I3C entries carry a flag byte selecting which of device class, manufacturer, part and extra fields participate plus those four fields and an opaque data pointer; FireWire entries carry match flags plus vendor, model, specifier and version codes plus a union offering either an integer or a pointer for driver data; IPACK entries carry format, vendor and device codes; ISA PnP entries carry card and device vendor and function codes plus driver context."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/i3c.h::I3C_MATCH_DCR","include/linux/device-id/i3c.h::I3C_MATCH_MANUF","include/linux/device-id/i3c.h::I3C_MATCH_PART","include/linux/device-id/i3c.h::I3C_MATCH_EXTRA_INFO","include/linux/device-id/ieee1394.h::IEEE1394_MATCH_VENDOR_ID","include/linux/device-id/ieee1394.h::IEEE1394_MATCH_MODEL_ID","include/linux/device-id/ieee1394.h::IEEE1394_MATCH_SPECIFIER_ID","include/linux/device-id/ieee1394.h::IEEE1394_MATCH_VERSION","include/linux/device-id/ssam.h::SSAM_MATCH_TARGET","include/linux/device-id/ssam.h::SSAM_MATCH_INSTANCE","include/linux/device-id/ssam.h::SSAM_MATCH_FUNCTION","include/linux/device-id/tb.h::TBSVC_MATCH_PROTOCOL_KEY","include/linux/device-id/tb.h::TBSVC_MATCH_PROTOCOL_ID","include/linux/device-id/tb.h::TBSVC_MATCH_PROTOCOL_VERSION","include/linux/device-id/tb.h::TBSVC_MATCH_PROTOCOL_REVISION"],"text":"Match selection bit sets use low powers of two with values one, two, four and eight in listed order, SSAM using only the first three: I3C distinguishes class, manufacturer, part and extra info; FireWire distinguishes vendor, model, specifier and version; SSAM distinguishes target, instance and function; Thunderbolt service distinguishes key, identifier, version and revision."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/input.h::input_device_id"],"text":"Input identification combines a flag word, four sixteen bit codes for bus type, vendor, product and version, ten capability bit sets sized to cover event, key, relative, absolute, miscellaneous, LED, sound, force feedback, switch and property spaces, and a driver information word."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_EV_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_KEY_MIN_INTERESTING","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_KEY_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_REL_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_ABS_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MSC_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_LED_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_SND_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_FF_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_SW_MAX","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_PROP_MAX"],"text":"Input capability upper bounds are thirty-one for events, one hundred thirteen as lowest interesting key with seven hundred sixty-seven as highest key, fifteen for relative and LED, sixty-three for absolute, seven for miscellaneous and sound, one hundred twenty-seven for force feedback, seventeen for switches and thirty-one for properties."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_BUS","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_VENDOR","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_PRODUCT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_VERSION","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_EVBIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_KEYBIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_RELBIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_ABSBIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_MSCIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_LEDBIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_SNDBIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_FFBIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_SWBIT","include/linux/device-id/input.h::INPUT_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_PROPBIT"],"text":"Input match selection uses one, two, four and eight for bus, vendor, product and version and successive powers of two from sixteen through eight thousand one hundred ninety-two for event, key, relative, absolute, miscellaneous, LED, sound, force feedback, switch and property bit sets."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/mdio.h::mdio_device_id","include/linux/device-id/mei_cl.h::mei_cl_device_id","include/linux/device-id/mhi.h::mhi_device_id","include/linux/device-id/mips_cdmm.h::mips_cdmm_device_id","include/linux/device-id/of.h::of_device_id","include/linux/device-id/parisc.h::parisc_device_id"],"text":"MDIO entries hold an identifier plus a mask; MEI client entries hold a fixed length name plus a little endian UUID, a version byte and driver context; MHI entries hold a fixed length channel name plus driver context; MIPS CDMM entries hold a single type byte; device tree entries hold name, type and compatible strings plus opaque data; PA-RISC entries hold hardware type, revision and version codes."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/i2c.h::I2C_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/i2c.h::I2C_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/pci.h::PCI_EPF_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/pci.h::PCI_EPF_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/platform.h::PLATFORM_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/platform.h::PLATFORM_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/mei_cl.h::MEI_CL_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/mei_cl.h::MEI_CL_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/mhi.h::MHI_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/rpmsg.h::RPMSG_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/slim.h::SLIMBUS_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/slim.h::SLIMBUS_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/spi.h::SPI_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/spi.h::SPI_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/spmi.h::SPMI_NAME_SIZE","include/linux/device-id/spmi.h::SPMI_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/ishtp.h::ISHTP_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/mdio.h::MDIO_MODULE_PREFIX","include/linux/device-id/of.h::of_device_id"],"text":"Fixed name capacities are twenty for I2C and PCI endpoint function, twenty-four for platform, thirty-two for MEI client, MHI channel, RPMSG, SLIMBus, SPI and SPMI, with device tree using thirty-two for name and type and one hundred twenty-eight for compatible; module prefixes use lower case bus letters followed by a colon, namely I2C initials, ISHTP initials, MDIO initials, letters m e i, word platform, word slim, letters s p i and letters s p m i."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/mei_cl.h::MEI_CL_VERSION_ANY","include/linux/device-id/parisc.h::PA_HWTYPE_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/parisc.h::PA_HVERSION_REV_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/parisc.h::PA_HVERSION_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/parisc.h::PA_SVERSION_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/rio.h::RIO_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/sdio.h::SDIO_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/serio.h::SERIO_ANY","include/linux/device-id/ssb.h::SSB_ANY_VENDOR","include/linux/device-id/ssb.h::SSB_ANY_ID","include/linux/device-id/ssb.h::SSB_ANY_REV","include/linux/device-id/typec.h::TYPEC_ANY_MODE"],"text":"Additional wildcards are 255 for MEI version, serio and SSB revision, 65535 for PA-RISC hardware version, RapidIO and SSB vendor and identifier, seven for Type-C mode, 255 for PA-RISC hardware type and revision, all bits set for SDIO and all bits set in thirty-two bits for PA-RISC software version."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/pci.h::pci_device_id","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::pcmcia_device_id","include/linux/device-id/platform.h::platform_device_id","include/linux/device-id/pnp.h::pnp_device_id","include/linux/device-id/pnp.h::pnp_card_device_id","include/linux/device-id/pnp.h::pnp_card_device_id.anon_1"],"text":"PCI entries hold vendor, device, subsystem vendor, subsystem device, class and class mask codes plus driver context and an override only flag; PCMCIA entries hold match flags, manufacturer and card codes, function identifiers, hashed and literal product strings, driver info and a configuration file name; platform entries pair a fixed length name with driver context; PnP entries pair an eight byte identifier with driver context, with card entries adding an array of up to eight device identifiers."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/pci.h::anon_1","include/linux/device-id/pnp.h::PNP_ID_LEN","include/linux/device-id/pnp.h::PNP_MAX_DEVICES","include/linux/device-id/tb.h::tb_service_id"],"text":"PCI override flag value is one; PnP identifier length and card device limit are both eight; Thunderbolt protocol key length is eight plus terminator."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_MANF_ID","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_CARD_ID","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_FUNC_ID","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_FUNCTION","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_PROD_ID1","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_PROD_ID2","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_PROD_ID3","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_PROD_ID4","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_DEVICE_NO","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_FAKE_CIS","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::PCMCIA_DEV_ID_MATCH_ANONYMOUS"],"text":"PCMCIA match selection uses successive powers of two from one through one thousand twenty-four for manufacturer, card, function identifier, function number, four product strings, device number, fake configuration and anonymous matching."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_VENDOR","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_PRODUCT","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_DEV_LO","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_DEV_HI","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_DEV_CLASS","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_DEV_SUBCLASS","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_DEV_PROTOCOL","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_INT_CLASS","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_INT_SUBCLASS","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_INT_PROTOCOL","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_INT_NUMBER"],"text":"USB match selection uses successive powers of two from one through one thousand twenty-four for vendor, product, device version bounds, device class triple and interface class triple plus interface number."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/rio.h::rio_device_id","include/linux/device-id/rpmsg.h::rpmsg_device_id","include/linux/device-id/sdio.h::sdio_device_id","include/linux/device-id/sdw.h::sdw_device_id","include/linux/device-id/serio.h::serio_device_id","include/linux/device-id/slim.h::slim_device_id","include/linux/device-id/spi.h::spi_device_id","include/linux/device-id/spmi.h::spmi_device_id","include/linux/device-id/ssam.h::ssam_device_id"],"text":"RapidIO entries hold device and vendor plus assembly counterparts; RPMSG, SPI and SPMI entries pair a fixed length name with driver context; SDIO entries hold class, vendor and device codes plus driver context; SoundWire entries hold manufacturer, part, version and class codes plus driver context; serio entries hold four single byte selectors for type, extra, identifier and protocol; SLIMBus entries hold manufacturer, product, index and instance codes plus driver context; SSAM entries hold match flags plus domain, category, target, instance and function selectors with driver context."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/device-id/ssb.h::ssb_device_id","include/linux/device-id/tb.h::tb_service_id","include/linux/device-id/tee_client.h::tee_client_device_id","include/linux/device-id/typec.h::typec_device_id","include/linux/device-id/ulpi.h::ulpi_device_id","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::usb_device_id"],"text":"SSB entries hold vendor, core and revision codes with explicit packing and alignment; Thunderbolt service entries hold match flags, a short protocol key string, protocol identifier version and revision plus driver context; TEE client entries hold only a UUID; Type-C entries hold a sixteen bit vendor identifier plus mode and driver context; ULPI entries hold vendor and product codes plus driver context; USB entries hold match flags, vendor product and version range, device and interface class triples, interface number and aligned driver information."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/mhi.h::MHI_DEVICE_MODALIAS_FMT","include/linux/device-id/mhi.h::MHI_EP_DEVICE_MODALIAS_FMT","include/linux/device-id/rpmsg.h::RPMSG_DEVICE_MODALIAS_FMT","include/linux/device-id/mdio.h::MDIO_ID_FMT","include/linux/device-id/mdio.h::MDIO_ID_ARGS","include/linux/device-id/ssb.h::SSB_DEVICE","include/linux/device-id/eisa.h::EISA_DEVICE_MODALIAS_FMT"],"text":"Modalias templates append a string placeholder to a bus tag and colon, using letters m h i for MHI host, letters m h i underscore e p for MHI endpoint, letters r p m s g for RPMSG and letters e i s a colon s for EISA; MDIO expands a thirty-two bit identifier into thirty-two single bit decimal digits and SSB offers a constructor from vendor, core and revision."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/eisa.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/hid.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/hv_vmbus.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/i2c.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/ieee1394.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/input.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/isapnp.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/ishtp.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/mcb.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/mei_cl.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/mhi.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/pci.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/pcmcia.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/platform.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/pnp.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/rpmsg.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/sdio.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/sdw.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/slim.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/spi.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/spmi.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/ssam.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/tb.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/typec.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/ulpi.h::kernel_ulong_t","include/linux/device-id/usb.h::kernel_ulong_t"],"text":"Many headers alias a word sized unsigned integer type used for driver private data, ensuring table entries carry either an integer or pointer sized value depending on architecture."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/device-id/dmi.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_DMI_H","include/linux/device-id/eisa.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_EISA_H","include/linux/device-id/fsl_mc.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_FSL_MC_H","include/linux/device-id/hda.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_HDA_H","include/linux/device-id/hid.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_HID_H","include/linux/device-id/hv_vmbus.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_HV_VMBUS_H","include/linux/device-id/i2c.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_I2C_H","include/linux/device-id/i3c.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_I3C_H","include/linux/device-id/ieee1394.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_IEEE1394_H","include/linux/device-id/input.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_INPUT_H","include/linux/device-id/ipack.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_IPACK_H","include/linux/device-id/isapnp.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_ISAPNP_H","include/linux/device-id/ishtp.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_ISHTP_H","include/linux/device-id/mcb.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_MCB_H","include/linux/device-id/mdio.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_MDIO_H","include/linux/device-id/mei_cl.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_MEI_CL_H","include/linux/device-id/mhi.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_MHI_H","include/linux/device-id/mips_cdmm.h::LINUX_DEVICE_ID_